      "difficulty_level": "H3",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author connects Weyl monomial equality to faithful polynomial action and lattice-path height polynomials, then proves the converse by balanced-subword commutation/flip normalizations. The seven-way characterization makes the local word-move relation exactly match the noncommutative algebra congruence and supplies an efficient equality test. Enumeration, c-Dyck restrictions, percolation/rook interpretations and other-algebra generalizations are complete context, not extra counts.",
